>joint</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">co</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 355.85 -39.37 L 386.64 -39.37"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 386.64 -39.37)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 369.67 -32.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.79em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.52" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.13)" width="11.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 523.66 -39.37 L 554.45 -39.37"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 554.45 -39.37)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 33.38 -55.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="154.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.9" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:11.13em;">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.9.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A) Semantic Analysis</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 301.96 4.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:19.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="273.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.10" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:19.79em;">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.10.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(B) Core Surgery &amp; Generation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>
<span id="S3.F1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overview of the Semantic Surgery Workflow.</span>
The process begins with <span id="S3.F1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A) Semantic Analysis</span>: <span id="S3.F1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">① Semantic Biopsy</span> analyzes the initial embedding <math id="S3.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce concept presence scores <math id="S3.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. These scores determine the set of active concepts, <math id="S3.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S3.F1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">② Co-Occurrence Encoding</span> then takes this set to form a unified removal direction <math id="S3.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This leads to <span id="S3.F1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(B) Core Surgery</span>: the scaled direction vector is subtracted from <math id="S3.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce a sanitized embedding <math id="S3.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is passed to the <span id="S3.F1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffusion Generator</span> (composed of a U-Net and VAE decoder) to generate an initial image.
For critical safety tasks, an optional <span id="S3.F1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">④ Visual Feedback Loop</span> (dashed red path) uses a vision detector to check for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP). If a concept is visually detected, a feedback signal updates the set of active concepts, triggering a refined, stronger surgery that leads to the final, clean image. (Note: The surgery step itself is implicitly step ③).
This entire framework is supported by a rigorous theoretical analysis (see Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a> for proofs), where we formally prove guarantees for <span id="S3.F1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completeness</span> (Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Completeness). ‣ G.2.1 Completeness (Erasure Guarantee) ‣ G.2 Proof of Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), <span id="S3.F1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Locality</span> (Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Locality). ‣ G.2.2 Locality (Fidelity Guarantee) ‣ G.2 Proof of Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and <span id="S3.F1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness</span> (Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Robustness as Lipschitz Continuity). ‣ G.2.3 Robustness (Resistance to Paraphrasing) ‣ G.2 Proof of Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The semantic manipulation capability of our method stems from the intrinsic linear structure of CLIP’s joint text-image embedding space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. This structure allows us to formalize concept removal through geometric operations that preserve semantic integrity.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The foundational insight originates from CLIP’s ability to encode semantic relationships as vector displacements as a language model<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. For example, the analogy <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext='\phi("\text{king}")-\phi("\text{man}")\approx\phi("\text{queen}")-\phi("\text{woman}")' display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>"</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>king</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>"</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>"</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>man</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>"</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>"</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>queen</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>"</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>"</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>woman</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>"</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi("\text{king}")-\phi("\text{man}")\approx\phi("\text{queen}")-\phi("\text{woman}")</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrates that semantic transformations can be modeled through vector arithmetic. Formally, for concept pairs <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c,d)</annotation></semantics></math> sharing analogous relationships (e.g., <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{king}:\text{man}\sim\text{queen}:\text{woman}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>king</mtext><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mtext>man</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mtext>queen</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mtext>woman</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{king}:\text{man}\sim\text{queen}:\text{woman}</annotation></semantics></math>), their embeddings satisfy:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(a)-\phi(b)\approx\phi(c)-\phi(d)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(a)-\phi(b)\approx\phi(c)-\phi(d),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">establishing the linear structure essential for semantic manipulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext='e_{\text{n}}=\phi("")' display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>"</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>"</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{n}}=\phi("")</annotation></semantics></math> denote the neutral reference embedding. Given an input prompt embedding <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}=\phi(p_{\text{input}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}=\phi(p_{\text{input}})</annotation></semantics></math> and a target concept <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> with embedding <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{erase}}=\phi(p_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{erase}}=\phi(p_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math>, to generalize Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) for concept removal, we introduce a binary presence indicator <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> that explicitly encodes whether the target concept exists in the input. This allows unified representation of both concept-containing (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>) and concept-free (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>) scenarios. Specifically, the analogical projection becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}-\rho e_{\text{erase}}\approx\phi(p_{\text{input}\setminus c})-\rho e_{\text{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>input</mtext><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}-\rho e_{\text{erase}}\approx\phi(p_{\text{input}\setminus c})-\rho e_{\text{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{input}\setminus c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>input</mtext><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{input}\setminus c}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the concept-free prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Rearranging terms yields the semantic surgery operator that maps <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the concept-removed space:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho(\underbrace{e_{\text{erase}}-e_{\text{n}}}_{\Delta e_{\text{erase}}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho(\underbrace{e_{\text{erase}}-e_{\text{n}}}_{\Delta e_{\text{erase}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which projects the input embedding <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> into the semantic subspace excluding concept <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\approx\phi(p_{\text{input}\setminus c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>input</mtext><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\approx\phi(p_{\text{input}\setminus c})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Co-Occurrence Encoding for Multi-Concept Erasure.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When extending single-concept removal to multiple targets <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, a naive approach would linearly superimpose individual concept offsets <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}\rho_{c_{i}}\Delta e_{c_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}\rho_{c_{i}}\Delta e_{c_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> following Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)’s paradigm. However, this strategy fails to account for semantic overlaps which will lead to uncontrollable semantic elimination. For instance, removing both "gull" and "sparrows" via separate offsets would excessively diminish avian features due to shared bird semantics. A qualitative comparison in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Qualitative Analysis of Co-Occurrence Encoding ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> (Fig. <a href="#A3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix C Qualitative Analysis of Co-Occurrence Encoding ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) visually demonstrates the superiority of this approach over naive vector summation, which leads to significant image degradation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The core solution lies in CLIP’s capacity to model composite semantics. We construct the co-erasure direction through existence-ordered composition:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}=\phi(p_{\text{co}})-e_{\text{n}},\quad p_{\text{co}}=\mathop{\bigoplus}\limits_{i=1}^{n}\left(\{p_{c_{i}}|c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}\}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}=\phi(p_{\text{co}})-e_{\text{n}},\quad p_{\text{co}}=\mathop{\bigoplus}\limits_{i=1}^{n}\left(\{p_{c_{i}}|c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}\}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\bigoplus}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⨁</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\bigoplus}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the concept concatenation operator of existing concepts (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> cases). For simplicity, we define it as comma-separated string concatenation. The composite prompt <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math> leverages CLIP’s contextual embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> to resolve semantic overlaps through phrase-level interaction, avoiding redundant subtraction of shared components.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{joint}}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{joint}}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the joint presence of all concepts selected in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{joint}}=\mathbb{I}\left(\bigwedge_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{S}}(\rho_{i}=1)\right)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\forall c_{i}\in\mathcal{S},\rho_{i}=1\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋀</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{joint}}=\mathbb{I}\left(\bigwedge_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{S}}(\rho_{i}=1)\right)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\forall c_{i}\in\mathcal{S},\rho_{i}=1\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the concept subset actually selected in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final operation preserves the form:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Semantic Surgery</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Projection Decomposition.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The theoretical foundation stems from the geometric relationship in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). We formalize concept intensity estimation through:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Concept Presence Projection)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For input embedding <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> and concept direction <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the presence intensity <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle}{\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle}{\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the ideal sanitized embedding, which is generally unobservable during inference and serves as a theoretical construct for this geometric interpretation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Angular Formulation)<span id="S3.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-normalized encoders with <math id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Defining <math id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}=\cos(e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}=\cos(e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}=\cos(e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}=\cos(e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx k(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx k(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Semantic Biopsy.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the sanitized embedding <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is unobservable during inference, the residual similarity <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be directly computed. The core objective of semantic biopsy is to estimate the concept intensity <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> solely from the observable <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. As established by our empirical findings (Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), the value of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is highly discriminative of whether the prompt implies concept presence or absence. We leverage this discriminability to calibrate an estimator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> that maps <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to a probabilistic presence score:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Statistical <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>-Separability)<span id="S3.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> values when prompt <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> contains the target concept, and <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> does not contain the concept. There exist a threshold <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, a separation margin <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a small tail probability <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}}[\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon]\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}_{\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}}[\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon]\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}}[\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon]\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}_{\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}}[\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon]\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This assumption, supported by empirical observations (Fig. <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Observed 𝛼_𝑐 Distributions and Separability. ‣ E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, Appendix <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>), states that with high probability, <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values from the two classes are separated by at least <math id="S3.Thmassumption1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for any target error bound <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, if we choose the sigmoid steepness parameter as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{\epsilon}{\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ln\left(\frac{1-\delta_{err}}{\delta_{err}}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{\epsilon}{\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=\frac{\epsilon}{\ln\left(\frac{1-\delta_{err}}{\delta_{err}}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the calibrated estimator <math id="Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma_{\text{sigmoid}}\left(\frac{\alpha_{c}-\beta}{\gamma}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sigmoid</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma_{\text{sigmoid}}\left(\frac{\alpha_{c}-\beta}{\gamma}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (concept present) and </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with probability </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{err}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>err</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{err}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (concept absent) and </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with probability </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{err}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>err</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{\mathrm{err}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This means that for inputs falling outside the uncertainty region <math id="Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, which happens with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each class, the estimator is <math id="Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>-close to the ideal binary presence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical Parameter Estimation.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The practical estimation of the decision threshold <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and sensitivity parameter <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is crucial for calibration. We determine <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> empirically by analyzing the separability of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions and fine-tune <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to balance classification sharpness and robustness. A detailed discussion of this process is provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Experimental Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Semantic Operation.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the set of calibrated presence scores <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each concept <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> (estimated via semantic biopsy, see Section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), we proceed with the multi-concept removal. First, we determine the subset of actively present concepts by applying a threshold <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}=\{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}\mid\hat{\rho}_{i}\geq\tau\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}=\{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}\mid\hat{\rho}_{i}\geq\tau\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-empty, we construct the corresponding co-occurrence prompt <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{co}}=\mathop{\bigoplus}_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}}p_{c_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{co}}=\mathop{\bigoplus}_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}}p_{c_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> (optionally ordering concepts by descending <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and compute its joint semantic direction <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}=\phi(p_{\text{co}})-e_{\text{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}=\phi(p_{\text{co}})-e_{\text{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Co-Occurrence Encoding for Multi-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To modulate the removal strength, we approximate the joint presence factor <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{joint}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{joint}}</annotation></semantics></math> (from Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In Co-Occurrence Encoding for Multi-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)) using the maximum estimated score among the active concepts:</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}=\max_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}}\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}=\max_{c_{i}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}}\{\hat{\rho}_{i}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The final semantic surgery operation is then performed using this approximated strength and the joint direction:</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{input}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{input}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}</annotation></semantics></math> is empty, the operation reduces to the identity, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{input}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{input}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This formulation naturally handles single concepts as a special case where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>active</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation</h3>

<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Latent Concept Persistence (LCP).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Despite the initial semantic surgery (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Semantic Operation. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)), yielding <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, where target concepts <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> are ideally absent from its direct semantics, these concepts may still be generated due to the U-Net’s visual priors being triggered by other concepts <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{im}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>im</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{im}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., "road" implying "trees"). The LCP risk, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>, quantifies this unintended visual resurgence for a set of visually detected persistent concepts <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> for formal definition).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To mitigate LCP, images generated using <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are evaluated by a vision detector <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding visual presence scores <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(k)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>im</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(k)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Concepts with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(k)}\geq\tau_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>im</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(k)}\geq\tau_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> form the visually active set <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which constitutes our LCP target set <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final set of concepts for removal, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{*}=\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}\cup\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{*}=\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}\cup\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}</annotation></semantics></math> is from initial semantic biopsy, Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), determines the LCP-specific co-occurrence prompt <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{co}}^{*}=\bigoplus_{c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}}p_{c_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{co}}^{*}=\bigoplus_{c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}}p_{c_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>, from which the direction <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is derived.
The joint removal strength, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, is determined by the maximum effective confidence among concepts in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, its effective score is <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}</annotation></semantics></math> (original semantic biopsy score), or <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}}\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>im</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}}\hat{\rho}_{\text{im}}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> (visually detected score scaled by a factor <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}}\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}}\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>). If <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is in both sets, its effective score is the maximum of these two.</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}=\max_{c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}}\{\text{effective\_score}(c_{j})\},\quad\text{or }0\text{ if }\mathcal{C}^{*}\text{ is empty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>effective_score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is empty</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}=\max_{c_{j}\in\mathcal{C}^{*}}\{\text{effective\_score}(c_{j})\},\quad\text{or }0\text{ if }\mathcal{C}^{*}\text{ is empty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The final, LCP-mitigated embedding <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is then computed by applying a comprehensive surgery to the original <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theoretical Support for Risk Reduction.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reduction in LCP risk via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback. ‣ 3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) is theoretically supported. By constructing <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to include visually persistent concepts <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, our surgery direction aims to counteract the U-Net’s LCP-inducing pathways. Under standard assumptions of directional alignment and local L-smoothness of the LCP risk function <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> (see Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>), applying the surgery with an appropriate strength <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> provably bounds the post-surgery risk (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (LCP Risk Bound via Directional Surgery). ‣ F.2 LCP Risk Reduction Theorem ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). This leads to risk reduction of the form <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})-C_{1}\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}+\mathcal{O}((\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*})^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})-C_{1}\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}+\mathcal{O}((\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*})^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The parameters <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}},\tau_{\text{sem}},\tau_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}},\tau_{\text{sem}},\tau_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> are tuned empirically to achieve a practical <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that balances risk reduction and fidelity (details in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Connection to Method Implementation and Empirical Validation ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The computational overhead of this optional two-pass mechanism is analyzed in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Ablation Study of Visual Feedback ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, where we show that its average inference time remains comparable to other training-free methods on practical safety benchmarks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate Semantic Surgery on diverse concept erasure tasks, focusing on <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">completeness</span> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 1st item ‣ Problem Formulation. ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)), <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">locality</span> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 2nd item ‣ Problem Formulation. ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)), and <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">robustness</span>. Robustness, crucial for practical completeness, measures erasure efficacy against paraphrased prompts unseen during configuration. We compare Semantic Surgery against state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods across these dimensions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tasks and Baselines.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate Semantic Surgery on five diverse erasure challenges. The first four are standard benchmarks: <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Object Erasure</span> (CIFAR-10 classes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>), <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Explicit Content Removal</span> (I2P dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>), and both <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Artistic Style</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Concept Celebrity Erasure</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. To specifically address a critical aspect of security, our fifth evaluation focuses on <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness Against Adversarial Attacks</span>, where we test our method’s resilience against both black-box (RAB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>) and white-box (UnlearnDiffAtk <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>) adversarial prompts. All experiments use Stable Diffusion v1.4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>. Our method is compared against state-of-the-art parameter-modifying (e.g., MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, Receler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>) and inference-time (SLD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, SAFREE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>) baselines. Detailed dataset provenances, evaluation metrics, and baseline configurations are provided in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Tasks, Datasets, and Metrics ‣ Appendix A Detailed Experimental Setup ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation Details.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our method’s key hyperparameters are set as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, with task-specific thresholds <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. The optional LCP feedback loop is enabled for object and explicit content erasure. To ensure unbiased evaluation in the object erasure task, we use an independent OWL-ViT detector <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> for final performance measurement. Further details on all hyperparameter choices and LCP configuration can be found in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Hyperparameter Settings and Visual Feedback Configuration ‣ Appendix A Detailed Experimental Setup ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compare Semantic Surgery against two classes of methods. Our primary comparison is against strong <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">parameter-modifying baselines</span>, which represent the state-of-the-art in erasure performance: ESD (-u and -x) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, UCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, AC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, Receler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, and MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. To provide a more comprehensive assessment, we also include a targeted comparison against contemporary <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">inference-time methods</span>, SLD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> and SAFREE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>, specifically on the critical I2P safety benchmark where the practical benefits of fast, training-free deployment are most paramount. For tasks adopting the MACE setup (Artistic Style, Multi-Concept Celebrity Erasure), results for MACE and other common baselines are taken directly from MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> to ensure fair comparison with their reported optimal performance. Other baseline results are reproduced using official code and recommended settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Object Erasure</h3>

<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental Setup.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate object erasure on the 10 categories of the CIFAR-10 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>. For each category, a model is configured to erase that specific target concept. We measure Efficacy (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>), Robustness (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>), and Locality (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>). <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the percentage of successful erasures for simple prompts (e.g., "A photo of {class}"). <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> measures erasure success for paraphrased prompts (e.g., "A sleek jetliner soaring through clear skies" for "airplane"), generated via ChatGPT as per Receler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>. <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is the generation accuracy for the nine non-target classes using their paraphrased prompts. Detection is performed by OWL-ViT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. Overall performance is summarized by the harmonic mean (H) of successful erasure rates (as percentages) and locality: <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=3/(1/(100-Acc_{E})+1/(100-Acc_{R})+1/Acc_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=3/(1/(100-Acc_{E})+1/(100-Acc_{R})+1/Acc_{L})</annotation></semantics></math>, where higher H is better.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Full evaluation of object erasure on all CIFAR-10 classes. <math id="S4.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>: Efficacy (lower is better), <math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>: Robustness (lower is better), <math id="S4.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>: Locality (higher is better), H: Harmonic Mean (higher is better). Full results for all 10 classes are in Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Additional Evaluation Results on CIFAR10 Classes ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>.</figcaption>
