</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Visual Feedback Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The visual feedback (LCP mitigation) module was employed for CIFAR-10 object erasure and I2P explicit content removal. If a targeted concept was detected above a predefined threshold in the initial generation, feedback reinforced the erasure in a second pass.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the I2P task, NudeNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> identifies exposed body parts (e.g., <span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BUTTOCKS_EXPOSED</span>, <span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FEMALE_BREAST_EXPOSED</span>). If the maximum detection score for any such element exceeded the threshold (e.g., 0.6), the erasure strength for all four targeted abstract concepts ("nude", "naked", "erotic", "sexual") was simultaneously increased in the second-stage generation, amplified by <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Dataset Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The datasets used for our experiments were sourced as follows:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CIFAR-10 Object Erasure:</span> We utilized the simple prompts and paraphrased prompts from the CIFAR-10 task setup of Receler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">I2P Explicit Content Removal:</span> This task used the standard I2P (Imagen Prompt Dataset) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, a common benchmark for evaluating safety in text-to-image models.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Artistic Style Erasure:</span> The list of artists targeted for style erasure was adopted from the experimental setup of MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, facilitating direct comparison.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Concept Celebrity Erasure:</span> Similarly, the set of celebrities for the multi-concept erasure task was also sourced from MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> to ensure fair comparability with prior work.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using established dataset configurations where possible aids in reproducibility and allows for more direct comparisons with existing methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ablation Study of Visual Feedback</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an ablation study to evaluate the impact of the Visual Feedback Adjustment module (Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>). Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix B Ablation Study of Visual Feedback ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the performance of Semantic Surgery with and without this component on the CIFAR-10 object erasure task (averaged over all classes) and the I2P explicit content removal task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Ablation study of the Visual Feedback Adjustment module. ‘Visual Feedback‘: <math id="A2.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the module is used, <math id="A2.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> indicates it is not. For CIFAR-10, metrics are averages over 10 classes. <math id="A2.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for CIFAR-10 corresponds to the <math id="A2.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> score defined in Sec 4.2. ‘Total‘ for I2P refers to the total count of nude images generated.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="3"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Config</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="3"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Visual Feedback</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="5">Task</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" colspan="4">CIFAR10</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">I2P</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Total</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">4</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">6.4</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">87.38</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">92.18</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">47</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">2</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">1.5</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">2.0</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">85.56</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">93.58</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">1</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results demonstrate the significant benefit of the visual feedback loop. On CIFAR-10, incorporating visual feedback improves erasure efficacy (<math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> from 4.0 to 1.5) and robustness (<math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> from 6.4 to 2.0) with only a marginal decrease in locality (<math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> from 87.38 to 85.56), leading to an overall improvement in the <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> score from 92.18 to 93.58. This slight drop in locality is primarily attributable to imperfections in the visual detector used for feedback. Specifically, we observed that the AOD detector occasionally misclassifies related but distinct concepts, for instance, identifying a "truck" as an "automobile." Such false positives incorrectly trigger a second-stage erasure surgery, which can inadvertently affect the generation of non-target concepts and thus slightly reduce the measured locality. This observation underscores the importance of employing a high-precision detector within the feedback loop to maximize its benefits while minimizing non-local effects.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The impact is even more pronounced for explicit content removal (I2P). Without visual feedback, 47 nude images are generated. With visual feedback, this number plummets to just 1, highlighting the module’s critical role in addressing Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) for sensitive concepts that may not be fully neutralized by semantic manipulation alone. The LCP scaling factor <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> (referred to as <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in the main text if Eq. <a href="#S3.E17" title="In LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback. ‣ 3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> was intended for this) was set to 1.0 for these experiments, balancing aggressive LCP correction with fidelity. For celebrity and style erasure tasks, the visual feedback loop was not employed due to minimal observed LCP risk (celebrity) or lack of a reliable detector (style), as noted in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference Time Analysis.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the computational overhead of the LCP visual feedback loop, we conducted a detailed timing analysis. The feedback loop is an on-demand, two-pass process; a second generation is triggered only if the detector identifies a persistent concept. Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Inference Time Analysis. ‣ Appendix B Ablation Study of Visual Feedback ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> benchmarks our method’s inference time per image against baselines.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Inference time analysis per image (50 steps) on a single NVIDIA RTX4090 GPU. The average LCP time for Semantic Surgery on the I2P task demonstrates its practical efficiency.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Scenario</th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Time per Image (seconds)</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">1. Baseline SDv1.4</th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">3.11 s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A2.T7.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inference-Time Methods</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">2. SLD</th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4.07 s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">3. SAFREE</th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.96 s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">4. <span id="A2.T7.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours (LCP disabled)</span></th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T7.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.21 s</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A2.T7.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Semantic Surgery with LCP</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">5. Ours (LCP worst-case, always 2-pass)</th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6.43 s</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T7.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T7.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">6. <span id="A2.T7.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours (LCP average on I2P task)</span></th>
<td id="A2.T7.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T7.2.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.09 s</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The analysis reveals three key points: (1) The core Semantic Surgery framework (LCP disabled) adds negligible overhead (3.21s vs. 3.11s for the baseline). (2) The "doubled time" scenario is a worst-case, not the norm. (3) In a practical, high-security application like the I2P task, the average inference time (4.09s) is comparable to other training-free methods like SLD and SAFREE, while providing vastly superior erasure completeness (as shown in main paper, Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Experimental Setup. ‣ 4.3 Explicit Content Removal ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). This highlights that the LCP module offers a highly effective and efficient trade-off for critical safety needs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Qualitative Analysis of Co-Occurrence Encoding</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our main paper (Sec. 3.1) introduces Co-Occurrence Encoding (Eq. 6) for robust multi-concept erasure. Figure <a href="#A3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix C Qualitative Analysis of Co-Occurrence Encoding ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> qualitatively compares it against a "Naive Approach" (summing individual erasure vectors) for erasing "dog" and "cat" from "dog and cat playing together."</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Co-Occurrence Encoding successfully removes both target animals while preserving the "playing together" action, often substituting them with plausible alternatives like children, thus maintaining the scene’s narrative. In contrast, the Naive Approach significantly degrades image quality and semantic coherence, leading to muddled imagery. This demonstrates Co-Occurrence Encoding’s advantage in neutralizing targets while protecting contextual integrity and image quality, unlike the naive method’s tendency to over-erase.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22851v1/Ablation_of_co-occurence_encoding.png" id="A3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:471/408;" width="471" height="408" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Qualitative comparison for multi-concept erasure ("dog", "cat"). Our Co-Occurrence Encoding (center) preserves semantics (e.g., "playing together" with children) while the Naive Approach (right) degrades image quality compared to the Original (left).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical Parameter Estimation.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> provides the theoretical basis for calibration using <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Practical application requires determining the parameters <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> for the estimator <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma_{\text{sigmoid}}((\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>sigmoid</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma_{\text{sigmoid}}((\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decision Threshold (<math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> This parameter corresponds to the threshold <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> described in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. It is empirically determined by analyzing the distributions of <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values for concept-present and concept-absent prompts to find a value that effectively separates them (see Appendix <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Observed 𝛼_𝑐 Distributions and Separability. ‣ E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). This <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> optimally centers the sigmoid’s decision boundary based on the observed data.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sensitivity Tuning (<math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The parameter <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> controls the steepness of the sigmoid function around <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. While Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> provides a theoretical construction for <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)) to achieve a specific error bound <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math> given an observed separation margin <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, in practice, <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is often fine-tuned empirically. This empirical tuning balances the sharpness of classification (smaller <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> for more decisive output near <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) with robustness to variations in <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> near the decision boundary and the desired level of confidence in the output <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. It typically involves evaluating performance on a validation set.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We analyzed sensitivity to hyperparameters <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (sigmoid steepness, main paper, Eq. 12) and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (concept presence threshold, main paper, Sec. 3.2) on CIFAR-10 object erasure (average over 10 classes, no visual feedback for this test). Defaults: <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> (global), task-dependent <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx-0.12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.12</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx-0.12</annotation></semantics></math> for CIFAR-10). For <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> sensitivity, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> was fixed at a near optimal value (e.g., -0.06).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (Sigmoid Steepness):</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Impact of 𝛾 (Sigmoid Steepness): ‣ Appendix D Experimental Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows metrics (<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E},Acc_{R},Acc_{L},H_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E},Acc_{R},Acc_{L},H_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> varies (log scale: 0.02 to 1.0). Stability across this range indicates low sensitivity to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, justifying our global choice of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.22851v1/impact_of_gamma_log_scale.svg" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/250;" width="429" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Impact of <math id="A4.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (Sigmoid Steepness, log scale) on Object Erasure (CIFAR-10) Performance Metrics. Metrics show high stability across tested <math id="A4.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> values.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (Concept Presence Threshold):</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Impact of 𝛽 (Concept Presence Threshold): ‣ Appendix D Experimental Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>’s impact. <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is crucial for erasure activation. <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates an optimal <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> range (around -0.12 to -0.06 here) balancing effective erasure (<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>) with high <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. This supports selecting <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions (main paper, Sec. 3.2).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.22851v1/impact_of_beta.svg" id="A4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/250;" width="429" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Impact of <math id="A4.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (Concept Presence Threshold) on Object Erasure (CIFAR-10) Performance Metrics. An optimal <math id="A4.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> range balances erasure effectiveness with semantic preservation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These analyses confirm that while <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> requires careful selection, robustness to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> variations enhances practicality.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (Concept Activation Threshold):</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The threshold <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> determines the minimum confidence score <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> required to activate the erasure for a concept <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. To evaluate its impact, we conducted an ablation study on the CIFAR-10 object erasure task (averaged over 10 classes, without visual feedback), with <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> fixed at their default values. Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Impact of 𝜏 (Concept Activation Threshold): ‣ Appendix D Experimental Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> presents the results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Ablation study for the concept activation threshold <math id="A4.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on CIFAR-10 object erasure. Performance is stable across a wide range of <math id="A4.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{Acc_{E}\downarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mi>𝑬</mi></msub></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{Acc_{E}\downarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{Acc_{R}\downarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mi>𝑹</mi></msub></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{Acc_{R}\downarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{Acc_{L}\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mi>𝑳</mi></msub></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{Acc_{L}\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{H\text{-score}\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-score</mtext></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{H\text{-score}\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.95</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">4.5</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">24.2</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">88.40</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">85.77</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T8.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5 (Default)</span></td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T8.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.0</span></td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T8.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.4</span></td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T8.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">87.38</span></td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T8.2.3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">92.18</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.05</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">4.0</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">3.5</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">84.90</td>
<td id="A4.T8.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">92.14</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results show that the model’s performance, particularly the overall H-score, is highly stable for <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> within a wide range of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.05,0.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.05,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math>. A very high threshold (e.g., 0.95) can degrade robustness (<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>) as it may fail to activate erasure for weaker semantic cues, while a very low threshold (e.g., 0.05) can slightly harm locality (<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) by being overly sensitive. Our chosen default of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> provides a strong balance, and the overall stability indicates that the method is not overly sensitive to this hyperparameter.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Geometric Interpretation of Ideal Concept Removal (Contextual Background)</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section outlines the geometric relationship for an idealized concept removal, as expressed in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Concept Presence Projection). ‣ Projection Decomposition. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and its Corollary. While our primary calibration mechanism (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) relies on the empirical discriminability of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values rather than directly inverting these equations, this geometric view provides context for why <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> can serve as an indicator of concept presence.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Concept Presence Projection). ‣ Projection Decomposition. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Concept Presence Projection).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For input embedding <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> and concept direction <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the presence intensity <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (as defined in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)) satisfies:</p>
<table id="A5.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle}{\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle}{\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the ideal sanitized embedding <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Linear Analogy Basis for Single-Concept Erasure. ‣ 3.1 Semantic Modeling in Text Embedding Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) in the main text, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Rearranging gives <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}=e_{\text{input}}-e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}=e_{\text{input}}-e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking the inner product of both sides with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\langle e_{\text{input}}-e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\langle e_{\text{input}}-e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\langle\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\langle\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\Delta e_{\text{erase}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle=\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and assuming <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we solve for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding Eq. (<a href="#A5.E19" title="In Theorem (Concept Presence Projection). ‣ E.1 Geometric Interpretation of Ideal Concept Removal (Contextual Background) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Corollary (Angular Formulation).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-normalized encoders where it can be assumed that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e_{\text{input}}^{\prime}\|</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., if <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> is small or re-normalization is applied), let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Defining <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}=\cos(e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}=\cos(e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}=\cos(e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}=\cos(e_{\text{input}}^{\prime},\Delta e_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="A5.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx k(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx k(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Concept Presence Projection). ‣ Projection Decomposition. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=(\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle)/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=(\langle e_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle-\langle e^{\prime}_{\text{input}},\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\rangle)/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u,v\rangle=\|u\|\|v\|\cos(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u,v\rangle=\|u\|\|v\|\cos(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=(\|e_{\text{input}}\|\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\alpha_{c}-\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}=(\|e_{\text{input}}\|\alpha_{c}-\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=(\|e_{\text{input}}\|\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\alpha_{c}-\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|^{2}=(\|e_{\text{input}}\|\alpha_{c}-\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e_{\text{input}}\|\approx\|e^{\prime}_{\text{input}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx\|e_{\text{input}}\|(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx\|e_{\text{input}}\|(\alpha_{c}-\alpha^{\prime})/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Defining <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\|e_{\text{input}}\|/\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math> gives Eq. (<a href="#A5.E20" title="In Corollary (Angular Formulation). ‣ E.1 Geometric Interpretation of Ideal Concept Removal (Contextual Background) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Relevance to Calibration:</span> These results illustrate that, ideally, a higher <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (when <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the concept, so <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is for a sanitized state) compared to a lower <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (when <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is like a sanitized state, so <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\approx\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\approx\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) is indicative of concept presence. Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> directly captures this empirically by observing the separation of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values based on whether the input prompt implies concept presence or absence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Empirical Support for <math id="A5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>-Separability (Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (Statistical <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>-Separability), which posits that <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}(p)=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{\text{erase}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}(p)=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{\text{erase}})</annotation></semantics></math> values for prompts containing a target concept are well-separated from those for prompts not containing it, is central to our calibration method. We provide strong empirical support for this assumption through a systematic prompt generation and evaluation process.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Systematic Prompt Generation.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously test the separability, we designed a ‘RobustPromptGenerator‘ (details of its configuration and generation logic are available in our supplementary code). This generator takes a configuration for an "anchor concept" (e.g., an object like "chair", a modifier like "red", a style like "Van Gogh", or sensitive content like "nude") and systematically generates three categories of prompts, each with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=100</annotation></semantics></math> unique instances:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Related Prompts (<math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> These prompts directly include the anchor concept (e.g., "a wooden <span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">chair</span> in studio photography"). Non-anchor components like scenes, other modifiers, and styles are varied randomly from predefined pools to ensure diversity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variant Prompts (<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{variants}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">variants</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{variants}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> These prompts replace the anchor concept with one of its pre-defined synonyms or close semantic variants (e.g., "an ergonomic <span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">seat</span> in 3D render" if "seat" is a variant of "chair"). Other components are varied similarly to related prompts. This group helps assess the robustness of <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to linguistic variations of the target concept.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unrelated Prompts (<math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{absent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">absent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{absent}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> These prompts replace the anchor concept with a pre-defined unrelated concept from a similar category (e.g., replacing "chair" with "lamp" if both are objects, or "red" with "blue" if both are colors), while attempting to keep other contextual components (scenes, styles, non-anchor modifiers/objects) consistent with those used for the related prompts where applicable, or varied from similar pools. This creates challenging negative samples that are contextually similar but semantically distinct regarding the anchor concept.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For each generated prompt <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute its embedding <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(p)</annotation></semantics></math> and then <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}(p)=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{\text{anchor}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>anchor</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}(p)=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{\text{anchor}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{anchor}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>anchor</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{anchor}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the pre-computed semantic direction for the specific anchor concept.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observed <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> Distributions and Separability.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The distributions of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values obtained from these prompt sets consistently demonstrate strong separability. Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Observed 𝛼_𝑐 Distributions and Separability. ‣ E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> illustrates typical outcomes for four diverse anchor concepts: "Object (Chair)", "Explicit Content (Nude)", "Style (Van Gogh)", and "Modifier (Red)".</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22851v1/evidence1.png" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/325;" width="452" height="325" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Illustrative <math id="A5.F6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions for different anchor concepts, demonstrating empirical separability.
For each subplot:
The <span id="A5.F6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">red distribution</span> (<math id="A5.F6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>, concept present) corresponds to <math id="A5.F6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values from <math id="A5.F6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math> (direct inclusion of the anchor concept).
The <span id="A5.F6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">yellow distribution</span> (<math id="A5.F6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>, concept variants) corresponds to <math id="A5.F6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values from <math id="A5.F6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{variants}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>variants</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{variants}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <span id="A5.F6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">blue distribution</span> (<math id="A5.F6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>, concept absent) corresponds to <math id="A5.F6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values from <math id="A5.F6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{absent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>absent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{absent}}</annotation></semantics></math> (unrelated prompts where the anchor concept is replaced).
The <span id="A5.F6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">green dashed line</span> indicates an empirically chosen threshold <math id="A5.F6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> that effectively separates the "concept absent" (blue) distribution from the "concept present" (red and yellow) distributions.
The clear separation between the blue distributions and the red/yellow distributions across diverse concept types strongly supports Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. The "concept variants" (yellow) generally align well with the "concept present" (red) distributions, indicating robustness to linguistic variations.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Observed 𝛼_𝑐 Distributions and Separability. ‣ E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values for <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{absent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>absent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{absent}}</annotation></semantics></math> (blue distributions, <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>) consistently cluster in a lower range of <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values for <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math> (red distributions, <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>) consistently cluster in a significantly higher range.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values for <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{variants}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>variants</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{variants}}</annotation></semantics></math> (yellow distributions, also considered <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math> for the purpose of concept presence) generally overlap substantially with the <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions, indicating that our <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{anchor}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>anchor</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{anchor}}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the core semantics despite linguistic variations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, for each anchor concept, there is a clear separation or minimal overlap between the <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{absent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>absent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{absent}}</annotation></semantics></math> (blue) distribution and the combined <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{present}}/P_{\text{variants}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>variants</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{present}}/P_{\text{variants}}</annotation></semantics></math> (red/yellow) distributions.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This observed separability allows for the robust determination of a threshold <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and a margin <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. For instance, the green dashed lines in Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Observed 𝛼_𝑐 Distributions and Separability. ‣ E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> represent empirically chosen <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> values. The margin <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> can then be identified as the distance from <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to the edge of the high-density regions of the separated distributions, and the tail probabilities <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> are observed to be very small. This systematic empirical validation across diverse concept types and prompt structures provides strong backing for our theoretical framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (Sigmoid Calibration)</h3>

<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for any target error bound <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, choosing <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext>logit</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math> ensures <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\text{sigmoid}((\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\text{sigmoid}((\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:
If <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)=1/(1+e^{-x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)=1/(1+e^{-x})</annotation></semantics></math> be the sigmoid function. The logit function is <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{logit}(p)=\ln(p/(1-p))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{logit}(p)=\ln(p/(1-p))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We want <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(X)\geq 1-\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(X)\geq 1-\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math> for positive classification, which implies <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\geq\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\geq\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We want <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(X)\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(X)\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math> for negative classification, which implies <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\leq\text{logit}(\delta_{err})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\leq\text{logit}(\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{logit}(\delta_{err})=-\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{logit}(\delta_{err})=-\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The parameter <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen as <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{\epsilon}{\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{\epsilon}{\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1:<span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Concept is present (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\geq\beta+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
The input to the sigmoid is <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{pres}}=(\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>pres</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{pres}}=(\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}-\beta\geq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}-\beta\geq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{pres}}\geq\epsilon/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>pres</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{pres}}\geq\epsilon/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting the chosen <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{pres}}\geq\frac{\epsilon}{\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>pres</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext>logit</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{pres}}\geq\frac{\epsilon}{\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma(X_{\text{pres}})\geq\sigma(\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err}))=1-\delta_{err}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>pres</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma(X_{\text{pres}})\geq\sigma(\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err}))=1-\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-1|\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>. This occurs with probability <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2:<span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Concept is absent (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\leq\beta-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
The input to the sigmoid is <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{abs}}=(\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>abs</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{abs}}=(\alpha_{c}-\beta)/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}-\beta\leq-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}-\beta\leq-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{\text{abs}}\leq-\epsilon/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>abs</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{abs}}\leq-\epsilon/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting the chosen <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{abs}}\leq\frac{-\epsilon}{\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=-\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})=\text{logit}(\delta_{err})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>abs</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext>logit</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{abs}}\leq\frac{-\epsilon}{\epsilon/\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})}=-\text{logit}(1-\delta_{err})=\text{logit}(\delta_{err})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma(X_{\text{abs}})\leq\sigma(\text{logit}(\delta_{err}))=\delta_{err}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>abs</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})=\sigma(X_{\text{abs}})\leq\sigma(\text{logit}(\delta_{err}))=\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})-0|\leq\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>. This occurs with probability <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proves that for inputs falling into the high-confidence regions (i.e., outside <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>), the estimator <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>-close to the ideal binary value. Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> ensures these high-confidence regions are indeed where most samples from <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> lie.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark on the uncertainty region <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta-\epsilon,\beta+\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
The theorem guarantees performance for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> values outside this uncertainty margin. Inside this margin, the value of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(\alpha_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> will smoothly transition between approximately <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{err}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{err}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> states that the probability of an <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> from either class <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> falling into the *other* class’s side of this margin (i.e., <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sim\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> having <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;\beta-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;\beta-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sim\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> having <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) is at most <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> is small, misclassifications or uncertain estimations are infrequent. The practical choice of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> aims to minimize errors within this region based on the observed distributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a formal theoretical framework for the LCP mitigation strategy described in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, based on standard assumptions from optimization theory.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Formal LCP Risk Definition and Assumptions</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) occurs when concepts <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, intended for removal and presumptively absent from the direct semantics of an initial surgically modified embedding <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (output of Eq. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Semantic Operation. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)), are nonetheless generated. This is attributed to the U-Net’s visual priors being triggered by other, semantically distinct concepts <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{im}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>im</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{im}}</annotation></semantics></math> present in or implied by <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the subset of concepts visually detected as persistent from images generated by <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the LCP risk function <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}:\mathbb{R}^{k}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}:\mathbb{R}^{k}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for an embedding <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> (which is assumed to be semantically sanitized w.r.t. <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> but may still cause their visual generation) as:</p>
<table id="A6.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e)=\mathbb{E}_{I\sim p_{\theta}(I|e)}\left[\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}}\mathbb{I}(c\in\text{Concepts}(I))\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Concepts</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e)=\mathbb{E}_{I\sim p_{\theta}(I|e)}\left[\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}}\mathbb{I}(c\in\text{Concepts}(I))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This measures the probability of at least one concept from <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> appearing. For analysis, we assume <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> or a suitable smooth surrogate is differentiable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The final LCP-mitigated surgery (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback. ‣ 3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>)) is <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where we map notation:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> (the embedding to which the full surgery is applied).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}=\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}=\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (the embedding after the LCP-aware surgery).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}=\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}=\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (the effective removal strength from Eq. (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback. ‣ 3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>)).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{surg}}=\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{surg}}=\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (the joint removal direction for <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{*}=\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}\cup\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{*}=\mathcal{C}_{\text{sem}}\cup\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The risk we aim to reduce is that observed at <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following standard assumptions:</p>
<ol id="A6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A1)</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Directional Alignment:</span> The chosen surgery direction <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-aligned with the negative gradient of the risk function <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, there exists a constant <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathcal{R}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathcal{R}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<table id="A6.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\geq\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\geq\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This implies that subtracting <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> moves the embedding in a direction that tends to reduce <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The construction of <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> (visually persistent concepts) strongly supports this alignment for mitigating LCP.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A2)</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L-Smoothness:</span> The gradient <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{R}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{R}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{a})-\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{b})\|\leq L\|e_{a}-e_{b}\|\quad\forall e_{a},e_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{a})-\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{b})\|\leq L\|e_{a}-e_{b}\|\quad\forall e_{a},e_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>LCP Risk Reduction Theorem</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LCP Risk Bound via Directional Surgery)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}=e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}=\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{0}-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}=\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}=e_{0}-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumptions <a href="#A6.I2.i1" title="item (A1) ‣ F.1 Formal LCP Risk Definition and Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(A1)</span></a> and <a href="#A6.I2.i2" title="item (A2) ‣ F.1 Formal LCP Risk Definition and Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(A2)</span></a>, the post-surgery risk <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{1})\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{1})\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For risk reduction (i.e., <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{1})&lt;\mathcal{R}(e_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{1})&lt;\mathcal{R}(e_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>), the effective step size <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}&lt;\frac{2\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|}{L\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}&lt;\frac{2\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|}{L\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">This result is a standard consequence of L-smoothness in optimization.
For an L-smooth function <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an update <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}=e_{0}+\delta e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}=e_{0}+\delta e</annotation></semantics></math>, Taylor’s theorem with a remainder bound (or descent lemma) gives:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{1})\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})+\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\delta e\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\delta e\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{1})\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})+\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\delta e\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\delta e\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">In our LCP mitigation surgery, the update is <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e=e_{1}-e_{0}=-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e=e_{1}-e_{0}=-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this into Eq. (<a href="#A6.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 LCP Risk Reduction Theorem ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(e_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(e_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})+\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})+\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|-\rho_{\text{eff}}\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we apply the Directional Alignment condition (Assumption <a href="#A6.I2.i1" title="item (A1) ‣ F.1 Formal LCP Risk Definition and Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(A1)</span></a>):
<math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\geq\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\geq\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since this term is preceded by a negative sign in Eq. (<a href="#A6.Ex6" title="Proof. ‣ F.2 LCP Risk Reduction Theorem ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>), we have:
<math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\rho_{\text{eff}}\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\leq-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\rho_{\text{eff}}\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0}),\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\rangle\leq-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this back gives:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(e_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(e_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}(e_{0})-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of Eq. (<a href="#A6.E24" title="In Theorem 3 (LCP Risk Bound via Directional Surgery). ‣ F.2 LCP Risk Reduction Theorem ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).
For <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to be less than <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we require the sum of the second and third terms on the right-hand side to be negative:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}&lt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\rho_{\text{eff}}\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|+\frac{L(\rho_{\text{eff}})^{2}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|^{2}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and assuming <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can divide by <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|+\frac{L\rho_{\text{eff}}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|&lt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|+\frac{L\rho_{\text{eff}}}{2}\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\implies\rho_{\text{eff}}&lt;\frac{2\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|}{L\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies\rho_{\text{eff}}&lt;\frac{2\eta_{\mathcal{R}}\|\nabla\mathcal{R}(e_{0})\|}{L\|\Delta e_{\text{surg}}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">This provides the condition on <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> for guaranteed risk reduction relative to <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Interpretation for LCP Mitigation Effect on <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
The theorem formally bounds <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> relative to <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(e_{\text{input}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(e_{\text{input}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The practical goal is to reduce the LCP risk <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> that was observed after the initial semantic-only surgery. The final surgery (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In LCP-Aware Concept Activation and Final Surgery via Visual Feedback. ‣ 3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>)) is specifically designed based on <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> (visually persistent concepts from <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus, <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen to counteract the factors leading to <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. While the direct proof applies to the change from <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the informed construction of the surgery ensures that <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is moved to a region of lower LCP risk compared to the state <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. The simplified statement in the main text, <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})-C_{1}\rho^{*}+\mathcal{O}((\rho^{*})^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{R}(\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime})-C_{1}\rho^{*}+\mathcal{O}((\rho^{*})^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, heuristically captures this intended consequence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Connection to Method Implementation and Empirical Validation</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The directional alignment (A1) is supported by constructing <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{surg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>surg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{surg}}</annotation></semantics></math> (our <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) to explicitly include visually persistent concepts <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>. L-smoothness (A2) is a common modeling assumption for deep learning systems. The step size <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> (our <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) is effectively controlled by the empirical tuning of <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{vis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>vis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{vis}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the estimated concept presence scores.
Qualitative examples demonstrating successful LCP removal provide visual confirmation of the method’s efficacy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22851v1/LCP.png" id="A6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/273;" width="476" height="273" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Qualitative illustration of LCP mitigation for the target concept "tree".
(<span id="A6.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left - Semantic Biopsy Only</span>): The input prompt is "a road", and the "tree" concept is targeted for erasure. Despite the prompt not semantically implying "tree", the initial semantic surgery (<math id="A6.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>s</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{s}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) fails to prevent trees from appearing, due to the U-Net’s strong prior associating roads with trees. Semantic biopsy alone does not detect this LCP issue as the prompt itself is "clean".
(<span id="A6.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right - Add Visual Feedback Adjustment</span>): After generating the image on the left, visual feedback detects the persistent "tree" concept. Our LCP-aware refined surgery (resulting in <math id="A6.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>final</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}_{\text{final}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) then incorporates this visual information. The subsequent image generation successfully removes the trees, yielding a scene consistent with only "a road". This visual improvement directly corroborates the risk reduction predicted by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (LCP Risk Bound via Directional Surgery). ‣ F.2 LCP Risk Reduction Theorem ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The example in Figure <a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.3 Connection to Method Implementation and Empirical Validation ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis of Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> clearly demonstrates that even when a concept (like "tree") is not semantically cued by the prompt ("a road") and might be missed by semantic-only analysis, LCP can cause its generation due to strong model priors. Our visual feedback mechanism effectively identifies such instances, and the subsequent LCP-aware surgery successfully removes the unintended concept, aligning with the theoretical prediction of risk reduction. This highlights the importance of the visual feedback loop in achieving comprehensive concept erasure.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides the formal theoretical framework supporting Semantic Surgery, linking our method to the desiderata of Completeness, Locality, and Robustness defined in the main paper (Sec. <a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="Problem Formulation. ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our analysis relies on three foundational principles, which are empirically validated in our work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Statistical Separability)<span id="A7.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any concept <math id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, the distribution of cosine similarities <math id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{c}=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{c}=\cos(\phi(p),\Delta e_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> for prompts containing the concept (<math id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) is statistically separable from the distribution for prompts not containing the concept (<math id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>). This is formally stated in the main paper’s Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Statistical 𝛼_𝑐-Separability). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and empirically validated in Appendix <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Empirical Support for 𝛼_𝑐-Separability (Assumption ) ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Framework and Empirical Support for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>. This property enables high-accuracy concept detection via our sigmoid calibration (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), ensuring <math id="A7.Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}-\rho_{\text{ideal}}|\leq\delta_{\text{err}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">err</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}-\rho_{\text{ideal}}|\leq\delta_{\text{err}}</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption G.2</span></span><span id="A7.Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Linear Erasure Error)<span id="A7.Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Vector subtraction provides a bounded approximation of ideal semantic removal. For an embedding <math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>, its ideal counterpart without concept <math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(p\setminus c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(p\setminus c)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the true presence <math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a small, empirically bounded error <math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(e-\rho\Delta e_{c})-\phi(p\setminus c)\|\leq\xi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(e-\rho\Delta e_{c})-\phi(p\setminus c)\|\leq\xi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This is grounded in the linear structure of CLIP’s embedding space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> and is validated by the high efficacy (<math id="A7.Thmassumption2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>) in our experiments.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption G.3</span></span><span id="A7.Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitz Continuity of the Generative Process)<span id="A7.Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Small perturbations in the embedding space lead to bounded changes in the probability of generating a concept. Let <math id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}(e)=\mathbb{E}_{I\sim p_{\theta}(I|e)}[\mathbb{I}(c\in\text{Concepts}(I))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Concepts</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}(e)=\mathbb{E}_{I\sim p_{\theta}(I|e)}[\mathbb{I}(c\in\text{Concepts}(I))]</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume <math id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="A7.Thmassumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g_{c}(e_{1})-g_{c}(e_{2})|\leq\lambda_{c}\|e_{1}-e_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g_{c}(e_{1})-g_{c}(e_{2})|\leq\lambda_{c}\|e_{1}-e_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Proof of Theoretical Guarantees</h3>

<section id="A7.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.2.1 </span>Completeness (Erasure Guarantee)</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Completeness)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}=e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the modified embedding for a concept <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumptions <a href="#A7.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption G.1 (Statistical Separability). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>-<a href="#A7.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption G.3 (Lipschitz Continuity of the Generative Process). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>, for a chosen safety threshold <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">safe</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>, if parameters are set such that <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}(\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\delta_{\text{err}}+\xi)&lt;\epsilon_{\text{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">err</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">safe</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}(\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\delta_{\text{err}}+\xi)&lt;\epsilon_{\text{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}(e^{\prime})\leq\epsilon_{\text{safe}}+O(\delta_{\mathrm{sep}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">safe</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sep</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}(e^{\prime})\leq\epsilon_{\text{safe}}+O(\delta_{\mathrm{sep}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{ideal}}=\phi(p\setminus c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{ideal}}=\phi(p\setminus c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the ideal embedding without concept <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. The error between our modified embedding <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and the ideal one is <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|=\|(e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}\Delta e_{\text{erase}})-e_{\text{ideal}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|=\|(e_{\text{input}}-\hat{\rho}\Delta e_{\text{erase}})-e_{\text{ideal}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
By applying the triangle inequality and adding/subtracting <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the true presence):</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}-e_{\text{ideal}})+(\rho-\hat{\rho})\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}}-e_{\text{ideal}})+(\rho-\hat{\rho})\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|(e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}})-e_{\text{ideal}}\|+\|(\rho-\hat{\rho})\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|(e_{\text{input}}-\rho\Delta e_{\text{erase}})-e_{\text{ideal}}\|+\|(\rho-\hat{\rho})\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\xi+|\rho-\hat{\rho}|\cdot\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\quad(\text{by Assumption \ref{assump:app_linear_error}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>by Assumption </mtext><mtext><a href="#A7.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption G.2 (Bounded Linear Erasure Error). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\xi+|\rho-\hat{\rho}|\cdot\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|\quad(\text{by Assumption \ref{assump:app_linear_error}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Assumption <a href="#A7.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption G.1 (Statistical Separability). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> and
Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> from the main paper, we know that <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho-\hat{\rho}|\leq\delta_{\text{err}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>err</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho-\hat{\rho}|\leq\delta_{\text{err}}</annotation></semantics></math> with
probability <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|\leq\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>err</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|\leq\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#A7.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption G.3 (Lipschitz Continuity of the Generative Process). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a> (Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g_{c}(e^{\prime})-g_{c}(e_{\text{ideal}})|\leq\lambda_{c}\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|\leq\lambda_{c}(\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>err</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g_{c}(e^{\prime})-g_{c}(e_{\text{ideal}})|\leq\lambda_{c}\|e^{\prime}-e_{\text{ideal}}\|\leq\lambda_{c}(\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, the ideal embedding <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\text{ideal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\text{ideal}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not contain concept <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}(e_{\text{ideal}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>ideal</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}(e_{\text{ideal}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}(e^{\prime})\leq\lambda_{c}(\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>err</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}(e^{\prime})\leq\lambda_{c}(\xi+\delta_{\text{err}}\|\Delta e_{\text{erase}}\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">If we choose parameters such that the right-hand side is less than <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>safe</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound holds. The term <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta_{\text{sep}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta_{\text{sep}})</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for the small probability that our presence estimation <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> falls outside the <math id="A7.SS2.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{err}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>err</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{err}}</annotation></semantics></math> error bound. The LCP mitigation module (main paper, Sec. <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Visual Feedback for Latent Concept Persistence (LCP) Mitigation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) further reduces any residual risk empirically.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.2.2 </span>Locality (Fidelity Guarantee)</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Locality)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any non-target concept <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\notin\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">erase</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\notin\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the change in its generation probability is bounded. With probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sep</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)\right|=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)\right|=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and with probability at most <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sep</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the impact is bounded by a negligible value <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)\right|\leq\kappa,\quad\text{where}\quad\kappa=\lambda_{d}M_{\text{co}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)\right|\leq\kappa,\quad\text{where}\quad\kappa=\lambda_{d}M_{\text{co}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e=e^{\prime}-e=-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e=e^{\prime}-e=-\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the surgery vector applied to the input embedding <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof proceeds by considering two cases based on whether the surgery is activated.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: Surgery is not activated (<math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e=0</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
This occurs when no target concepts are detected in the input prompt, i.e., <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the activation threshold). From Assumption <a href="#A7.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption G.1 (Statistical Separability). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sigmoid Calibration with High Confidence). ‣ Semantic Biopsy. ‣ 3.2 Semantic Surgery ‣ 3 Method ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the probability of a false positive detection for any single concept is low. Thus, the probability of incorrectly activating the surgery when no target concepts are present is bounded by <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, with a high probability of at least <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>, no surgery is applied. In this case, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}=e</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the impact on any non-target concept <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is zero:</span></span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)|=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)|=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: Surgery is activated (<math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
This occurs with a low probability of at most <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> when no target concept is present, or when a target concept is correctly detected. By Assumption <a href="#A7.Thmassumption3" title="Assumption G.3 (Lipschitz Continuity of the Generative Process). ‣ G.1 Core Theoretical Framework and Assumptions ‣ Appendix G Theoretical Guarantees for Semantic Surgery ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a> (Lipschitz continuity), the change in the generation probability of concept <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</span></span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)|\leq\lambda_{d}\|e^{\prime}-e\|=\lambda_{d}\|\delta e\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g_{d}(e^{\prime})-g_{d}(e)|\leq\lambda_{d}\|e^{\prime}-e\|=\lambda_{d}\|\delta e\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can bound the norm of the surgery vector. Since <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and letting <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{co}}=\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{co}}=\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}\|</annotation></semantics></math> be the norm of the co-occurrence direction vector (which is bounded for a given set of concepts), we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta e\|=\|\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}\|\leq M_{\text{co}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>joint</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta e\|=\|\hat{\rho}_{\text{joint}}\Delta e_{\text{co}}\|\leq M_{\text{co}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the maximum impact in this case is bounded by <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\lambda_{d}M_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\lambda_{d}M_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">While this provides a formal bound, the practical impact is typically much smaller. This is because the surgery vector <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed from target concepts and is thus nearly orthogonal to the semantic direction <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of a distinct, unrelated concept <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. This near-orthogonality ensures that the vector subtraction primarily affects semantic components related to <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>erase</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{erase}}</annotation></semantics></math>, minimizing collateral impact on <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion.<span id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Combining both cases, the expected impact on a non-target concept is negligible. The most common scenario (with probability <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> for concept-absent prompts) results in zero impact. In the less frequent case of an incorrect activation, the impact is bounded by a small constant <math id="A7.SS2.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the locality of our method.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.2.3 </span>Robustness (Resistance to Paraphrasing)</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robustness as Lipschitz Continuity)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Semantic Surgery operator <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}(e)=e-\hat{\rho}(e)\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}(e)=e-\hat{\rho}(e)\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz continuous. That is, there exists a constant <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any embedding <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> and a sufficiently small perturbation <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta e</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{T}(e+\delta e)-\mathcal{T}(e)\|\leq L\|\delta e\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{T}(e+\delta e)-\mathcal{T}(e)\|\leq L\|\delta e\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}=e</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{2}=e+\delta e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{2}=e+\delta e</annotation></semantics></math>. We need to bound <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(e_{2}-\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2}))-(e_{1}-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1}))\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(e_{2}-\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2}))-(e_{1}-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1}))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(e_{2}-e_{1})-(\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1}))\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(e_{2}-e_{1})-(\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1}))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|e_{2}-e_{1}\|+\|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|e_{2}-e_{1}\|+\|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta e\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta e\|</annotation></semantics></math>. We focus on the second term by adding and subtracting <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|\leq|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})\|+|\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|\leq|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})\|+|\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let’s bound each component:</span></p>
<ol id="A7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(e)=\sigma((\cos(e,\Delta e_{c})-\beta)/\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(e)=\sigma((\cos(e,\Delta e_{c})-\beta)/\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is a composition of locally Lipschitz functions. The cosine similarity <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos(e,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos(e,v)</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz w.r.t. <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>, and the sigmoid <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is globally Lipschitz. Thus, <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz with some constant <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\leq L_{\rho}\|e_{2}-e_{1}\|=L_{\rho}\|\delta e\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(e_{2})-\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|\leq L_{\rho}\|e_{2}-e_{1}\|=L_{\rho}\|\delta e\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The concept direction norm <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by some constant <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The co-occurrence direction <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> is also locally Lipschitz. This is because it depends on which concepts exceed the threshold <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, but within a neighborhood where the active set of concepts does not change, <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta e_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta e_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant. At the boundaries, it has jump discontinuities, but we consider a neighborhood where it is stable. For simplicity, assume it is locally Lipschitz with constant <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|\leq L_{\text{co}}\|\delta e\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{2})-\Delta e_{\text{co}}(e_{1})\|\leq L_{\text{co}}\|\delta e\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\rho}(e_{1})|</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by 1.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these bounds back:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|\leq\|\delta e\|+(L_{\rho}\|\delta e\|)M+(1)(L_{\text{co}}\|\delta e\|)=(1+ML_{\rho}+L_{\text{co}})\|\delta e\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{T}(e_{2})-\mathcal{T}(e_{1})\|\leq\|\delta e\|+(L_{\rho}\|\delta e\|)M+(1)(L_{\text{co}}\|\delta e\|)=(1+ML_{\rho}+L_{\text{co}})\|\delta e\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1+ML_{\rho}+L_{\text{co}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>co</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1+ML_{\rho}+L_{\text{co}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have shown that <math id="A7.SS2.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz continuous, which proves the theorem. This directly guarantees that small changes in input embeddings lead to proportionally small changes in the output, ensuring robustness.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Additional Evaluation Results on CIFAR10 Classes</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the complete evaluation results for object erasure across all 10 CIFAR-10 classes, supplementing the selected results presented in the main paper (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Experimental Setup. ‣ 4.2 Object Erasure ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). The metrics <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> (Efficacy), <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (Robustness), <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Acc_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Acc_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> (Locality), and <math id="A8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> (Harmonic Mean) are defined in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. As shown in Table <a href="#A8.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix H Additional Evaluation Results on CIFAR10 Classes ‣ Semantic Surgery: Zero-Shot Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, Semantic Surgery consistently demonstrates strong performance across all classes, achieving the highest average <math id="A8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> score.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T9" class="ltx_table">
